<title>CZECH REPUBLIC: TENNIS-PAES BRINGS INDIA LEVEL IN DAVIS CUP TIE.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-PAES BRINGS INDIA LEVEL IN DAVIS CUP TIE.</headline>
<dateline>PRIBRAM, Czech Republic 1997-02-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Results from the</p>
<p>opening singles matches in the Davis Cup World Group first</p>
<p>round tie between the Czech Republic and India on Friday:</p>
<p>(Czech names first)</p>
<p>Petr Korda beat Mahesh Bhupathi 6-3 6-7 (2-7) 6-1 6-2</p>
<p>Jiri Novak lost to Leander Paes 2-6 3-6 7-6 (7-5) 3-6</p>
<p>Saturday's doubles (1400 GMT):</p>
<p>Martin Damm/Pavel Vizner v Paes/Bhupathi</p>
<p>Sunday's reverse singles (1300 GMT):</p>
<p>Korda v Paes</p>
<p>Novak v Bhupathi</p>
</text>
